WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.447
Fifty distinct findings mapped to the Criminal Code of Canada and the Rome Statute of the International Criminal Court.

00:00:06.397 --> 00:00:09.534
Breach of trust: Section 122.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:12.659
Fraud on government: Section 121.

00:00:12.659 --> 00:00:20.193
Conflict of interest: Section 121, subsection 1-c. Foreign interference: Section 76 — treason.

00:00:20.193 --> 00:00:24.965
Crimes against humanity allegations mapped to Article 7 of the Rome Statute.

00:00:24.965 --> 00:00:30.045
Individual criminal responsibility documented for more than twelve named individuals.

00:00:30.045 --> 00:00:35.806
Total potential liability: life imprisonment for conspiracy, twenty years for breach of trust.

00:00:35.806 --> 00:00:38.874
Every finding is sourced from public records.

00:00:38.874 --> 00:00:40.829
Hansard transcripts.

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:43.079
Lobbying registrations.

00:00:43.079 --> 00:00:44.806
Court filings.

00:00:44.806 --> 00:00:46.999
Auditor General reports.

00:00:46.999 --> 00:00:49.363
The evidence was always there.

00:00:49.363 --> 00:00:51.943
It was in fifty different places.

00:00:51.943 --> 00:00:54.227
This page puts it in one.
